You need to implement a full Blazor ShipmentTracker application. The project is at `/tmp/sv-def46ec4bdef476fb5894767d4f076e4/ShipmentTracker/`.

The solution already has:
- `ShipmentTracker/` (server project, .NET 11 preview, net11.0 TFM)
- `ShipmentTracker.Client/` (WASM client project)
- Individual auth with Identity and SQLite
- `ApplicationDbContext` in `Data/` folder (currently empty except Identity)
- The server csproj uses preview packages version `11.0.0-preview.3.26207.106`

Here's EXACTLY what to implement. Do all steps:

## Step 1: Create ShipmentTracker.Shared class library

Create dir `/tmp/sv-def46ec4bdef476fb5894767d4f076e4/ShipmentTracker/ShipmentTracker.Shared/`

Create `ShipmentTracker.Shared.csproj`:
```xml
<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net11.0</TargetFramework>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
  </PropertyGroup>
</Project>
```

Create `Shipment.cs`:
```csharp
namespace ShipmentTracker.Shared;

public class Shipment
{
    public int Id { get; set; }
    public string TrackingNumber { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Origin { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Destination { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public ShipmentStatus Status { get; set; }
    public DateTime CreatedAt { get; set; }
    public DateTime? EstimatedDelivery { get; set; }
    public DateTime? ActualDelivery { get; set; }
    public string CustomerEmail { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Description { get; set; } = string.Empty;
}

public enum ShipmentStatus
{
    Pending,
    PickedUp,
    InTransit,
    OutForDelivery,
    Delivered,
    Cancelled
}
```

Create `ShipmentDto.cs`:
```csharp
using System.ComponentModel.DataAnnotations;

namespace ShipmentTracker.Shared;

public class ShipmentDto
{
    public int Id { get; set; }
    public string TrackingNumber { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    [Required(ErrorMessage = "Origin is required")]
    public string Origin { get; set; } = string.Empty;

